WEBVTT

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:10.450
Earth, the 23rd century, a time of robots and aliens, and of destruction and terror.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:17.800
Can the Galactic Patrol, defender of the United Planets, stop the evil computer, Umbra?

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:19.920
You bet they can.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:29.300
Meet Rob Simmons, the secret inventor of Heisty Bono, Mighty Tor, Versatile Boat, Elusive Boo.

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:34.330
Hold the master of the elements and crush the Metal Muncher.

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.800
Super robots forging together at Rob's command to form...

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:43.700
Mighty Robots, champions of the universe.

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:41.610
Evangelion No.1

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:42.950
Lift off!

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:46.610
Shinji-kun.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:01.380
I walked.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:38.750
What about the Eva's defense system?

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:40.130
The signal is not working.

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:41.620
The field is not open.

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:43.000
Is it no good?

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:02.290
A crack has occurred in the tank!

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:03.320
The armor is no longer...

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:13.420
It's no longer...

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:14.420
The armor is no longer...

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.500
Damaged.

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:16.500
Invincible.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.500
The special nerves are gradually moving.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:18.330
The special nerves are gradually moving.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:19.890
The private...

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:21.280
The private...

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:54.740
It's a strange angel.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:13.070
It's the same as what happened 15 years ago.

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:16.910
We'll be able to visit without any trouble.

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:23.340
We can say that it's a good thing that our advance investment didn't go to waste.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.520
I still don't understand that.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:30.000
If it doesn't help, we'll have to do something about it.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.320
It's the same as nothing.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:34.600
Now that it's become a fact that it's already been discovered,

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:44.600
it will be troublesome if you don't get all the information operation and NERV operation done properly and quickly.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:47.700
We have already dealt with that matter.

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.350
Don't worry.

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:54.530
The second case of the Ryoji era...

00:04:54.530 --> 00:04:56.710
In this case...

00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:59.280
The announcement is scenario B-22, huh?

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:02.320
The truth is still in the dark, isn't it?

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:06.310
The Ministry of Defense was happy to hear that we were finally able to do our job.

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:08.880
We're happy too, aren't we?

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:12.450
I wonder. Are you all really scared?

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.370
Of course.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:17.110
Well, that's true.

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:22.980
However, Ikari-kun, can you use NERV a little better?

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:30.000
The repair cost of Unit 0, which you guys broke with the Uijin, has been reduced by one country.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:34.400
If you ask me, that toy is the one you gave to your son, isn't it?

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.690
People, time, and money.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:41.100
How much do you think you can make with all of them?

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:44.180
Besides, your job is not just this.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:45.760
The Human Saving Project.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:48.260
This is your duty.

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:49.630
That's right.

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:55.090
That project is our only hope in this desperate situation.

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:56.490
Our only hope.

00:05:56.490 --> 00:06:00.000
In any case, the project that we are working on,

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.390
I cannot accept the delay in the schedule.

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:06.300
Let's move on to the budget.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:09.080
Then, the rest is the work of the committee.

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:13.890
Ikari-kun, thank you for your hard work.

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:17.440
Ikari, you can't go back.

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:22.590
I know.

00:06:22.590 --> 00:06:24.420
Humans don't have time.

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:54.350
Kool-Aid is the way of the human race.

00:06:54.350 --> 00:06:56.810
That's exactly the victory of science.

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:58.230
Shinji-kun has noticed.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.900
How about your brother?

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:02.110
He is fine.

00:07:02.110 --> 00:07:04.220
He seems to be a little confused in his memory.

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:06.470
Could it be that he has a mental health problem?

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:08.900
He doesn't seem to be worried about that.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.620
I see...

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:13.200
That's right.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.200
It was all of a sudden.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:16.120
It's not impossible.

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:19.170
It took a lot of pressure on his brain nerves.

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:22.240
Isn't it a mistake of the heart?

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:54.450
If Ever and this town can move completely, we might be able to make it.

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:56.370
Are you going to defeat the Apostles?

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:58.110
You're as easygoing as ever.

00:07:58.110 --> 00:07:58.840
Oh!

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:00.000
Hopeful observation is...

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:02.310
A must-have item for you to keep on living.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:05.300
That's right.

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:07.300
That's a good place for you, too.

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:49.590
It's good, isn't it?

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.230
Instead of living together.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:53.310
For Ikari and the others,

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:56.630
it's natural for them to live without each other.

00:08:56.630 --> 00:08:59.600
Rather, it's more unnatural to be together.

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:02.630
Alone?

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:03.710
That's right.

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:06.410
His room will be the sixth block from here.

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:07.970
No problem.

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:09.060
Yes.

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:11.570
Is that okay?

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:12.910
Shinji-kun.

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:13.840
It's okay.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:18.020
It's the same everywhere alone.

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:19.360
What did you say?

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:24.210
That's why Shinji-kun decided to live with me.

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:26.090
I also got permission from above.

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:27.740
You don't have to worry about it.

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:29.250
I won't touch the child.

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:30.000
Of course not.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:32.020
What are you thinking about?

00:09:32.020 --> 00:09:35.890
You still don't understand Jouku.

00:09:35.890 --> 00:09:45.040
What are you talking about?

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:49.040
Of course, a welcome party of a new comrade.

00:09:49.040 --> 00:09:56.010
Are you moving?

00:09:56.010 --> 00:10:00.000
I didn't think this place would really be a battlefield.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.000
I wouldn't have been able to do that if it wasn't for you.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.810
That's true...

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:05.870
My husband also told me to get rid of the children and me.

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:08.040
Get rid of them...

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:12.190
No matter how old you are, you won't be able to do anything.

00:10:12.190 --> 00:10:15.040
I just remembered what happened yesterday...

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:22.660
I'm sorry, but...

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:24.830
I'm going on a little trip.

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:26.110
Where are you going?

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:28.250
I'm going to Iitakara.

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:38.610
Somehow, it's a lonely town.

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:41.430
It's time.

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:32.690
Shintokyo City, our city.

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:38.810
And the city you protected.

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:55.450
I think it's already here.

00:11:57.010 --> 00:12:00.000
Actually, I just moved to this city the other day.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.160
See you later.

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:04.080
Come in.

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:06.570
Excuse me.

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:10.580
Shinji, this is your house.

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:19.570
I'm back.

00:12:19.570 --> 00:12:20.880
Welcome back.

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:28.000
It's a bit messy, but don't worry about it.

00:12:30.350 --> 00:12:31.600
This is...

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:34.040
Chocchi?

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:37.780
Put the food in the fridge!

00:12:37.780 --> 00:12:39.350
Yes!

00:12:39.960 --> 00:12:42.120
Fruits...

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:43.220
Snacks...

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:45.690
And beer.

00:12:45.690 --> 00:12:52.360
What kind of life is this?

00:12:52.360 --> 00:13:00.000
That's fine!

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:02.060
I think you're still asleep.

00:13:02.060 --> 00:13:04.220
I'm asleep?

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:07.340
Did you say that?

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:08.780
I'll eat it.

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:23.360
As I thought, life is like living for this moment.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.700
Is that so?

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:27.430
It's pretty good, though it's instant.

00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:29.190
No, um...

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.570
I'm not used to this kind of meal...

00:13:31.570 --> 00:13:32.830
You can't do that!

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:34.710
You're going to hate me!

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:37.170
No, that's not it!

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:39.060
Um...

00:13:39.060 --> 00:13:40.980
It's fun, isn't it?

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:44.330
You're going to eat with other people like this, right?

00:13:44.330 --> 00:13:46.800
Yes.

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:51.730
Then, let's move on to the next one.

00:13:51.730 --> 00:13:53.910
Rock, paper, scissors!

00:13:53.910 --> 00:13:56.280
Scissors!

00:14:02.170 --> 00:14:02.690
All right!

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:06.850
Now that we've decided on our life, it's all good, right?

00:14:06.850 --> 00:14:08.290
Yes.

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:11.820
Well, from today on, this is your house.

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:14.650
You don't need to hold back at all.

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:15.880
Yes.

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:19.680
Geez, "yes, yes, yes, yes" is so old-fashioned.

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:21.480
Hey, where are you going?

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:22.220
I'll kick you!

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:23.760
Yes, I'll kick you!

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:25.240
Yes.

00:14:25.240 --> 00:14:26.860
Well, that's fine.

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:28.800
If you don't like it, you can go to the bathroom.

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:34.420
Don't worry. A professional is a choice of life.

00:15:05.280 --> 00:15:06.640
The name is "Pen-Pen"

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:08.380
To another person's cohabitation

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:10.120
Rather than that

